/* TEMPLATE for the licensed display font (committed; the real fonts.css and the
   font files are gitignored).
 *
 * The app's heading face is "Captain Edward" by SimpleBits
 * (https://simplebits.shop/collections/fonts) — a licensed font that is NOT
 * redistributed with this repository.
 *
 * To enable it locally or on a deployment:
 *   1. Buy/download Captain Edward.
 *   2. Drop the web fonts into this directory (web/static/fonts/):
 *        CaptainEdward-Regular.woff2  CaptainEdward-Regular.woff
 *        CaptainEdward-Bold.woff2     CaptainEdward-Bold.woff
 *   3. Copy this file to `fonts.css` (same dir).
 *
 * Without it, app.html's font <link> 404s harmlessly and --font-display falls back
 * to the serif stack in app.css — the app still looks correct, just with a system
 * serif for headings.
 *
 * NOTE: the url()s below are RELATIVE (no leading slash) so they resolve correctly
 * whether the site is served at the domain root or under a sub-path (e.g. /atlas).
 * If you maintain your own fonts.css, keep the urls relative too.
 */
@font-face {
	font-family: 'Captain Edward';
	src:
		url('CaptainEdward-Regular.woff2') format('woff2'),
		url('CaptainEdward-Regular.woff') format('woff');
	font-weight: 400;
	font-style: normal;
	font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
	font-family: 'Captain Edward';
	src:
		url('CaptainEdward-Bold.woff2') format('woff2'),
		url('CaptainEdward-Bold.woff') format('woff');
	font-weight: 700;
	font-style: normal;
	font-display: swap;
}
